I am still talking to my mother.
Mother's face is very happy.
"Maya, tell me that story too," mother says.
"You? You were right there!" I say, laughing.
"Even so, I want to hear it from you," mother says.
I say yes.
I start the story again.
"That night the plane landed in Mumbai…"
Mother smiles.
She remembers that day well.
"That day was very special," mother says.
"Did you tell them about Mexico too?" she asks.
"No, mother," I say.
"Only the Mumbai part."
Mother becomes a little sentimental.
"Tell me that story again, Maya," mother says.
"That morning of your journey."
"When we said goodbye at the airport."
I remember that day too.
I smile and say yes.
I start my story again for her.
